-- title:
--   Newvector in the cyclic span from local GL₃timesGL₂ functional equations
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ is a number field, equipped with an algebra structure of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ on $\mathcal{O}_K$ that is integral, and `hdeg` requires $[K:\mathbb{Q}]=3$. Further, $\mu$ is a group homomorphism from the ideles $(\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times}$ to $\mathbb{C}^{\times}$, and `hμ` asserts `IsAdmissibleTwist`: $\mu$ is trivial on the principal ideles $K^{\times}$, continuous, and of absolute value $1$ at every idele. The place $v$ is a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$; write $N=$ `Ideal.absNorm v.asIdeal` for the absolute norm of $v$, $\mathbb{Q}_v$ for `v.adicCompletion ℚ`, $\psi_v=$ `psiLocal ℚ v` for the standard local additive character at $v$, and
--   $$\ell \;=\; \mathrm{inducedLevelAt}\,K\,\mu\,v\;=\;\sum_{\mathfrak{P}\mid v} f(v,\mathfrak{P})\cdot a\big(\mu_{\mathfrak{P}}\big),$$
--   the sum over the primes $\mathfrak{P}$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$ lying under $v$ of the inertia degree times the conductor exponent `conductorExponentAt` of the local character `localChar μ 𝔓`. The hypothesis `hv` (`IsTwistRamifiedAbove`) asserts that some $\mathfrak{P}$ above $v$ has $\mu$ ramified at $\mathfrak{P}$ (i.e. `IsUnramifiedCharAt μ 𝔓` fails), and `hvr` asserts that `IsRamifiedIn K v` fails, i.e. every $\mathfrak{P}$ above $v$ has ramification index $1$. Finally set $E=$ `inducedEulerPoly ℚ (inducedCoeff K μ) v` and $E^{\vee}=$ `inducedEulerPoly ℚ (inducedCoeff K μ⁻¹) v`, the finite products $\prod_{\mathfrak{P}\mid v}\big(1-c(\mathfrak{P})X^{f(v,\mathfrak{P})}\big)$ with $c(\mathfrak{P})$ equal to the value of the relevant character on the uniformiser idele at $\mathfrak{P}$ when that character is unramified at $\mathfrak{P}$, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   The datum on $\mathrm{GL}_3$ is a function $W_0$ on `LocalGL3 v` $=\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$, and `h₀` asserts `IsLocalWhittakerDatum v ψ_v⁻¹ W₀`, which consists of six clauses: $W_0(u(x,y,z)g)=\psi_v^{-1}(x+y)\,W_0(g)$ for all upper unipotent $u(x,y,z)$ and all $g$; $W_0(1)=1$; the uniqueness-of-Whittaker-functional statement `HasWhittakerMultOne` for the cyclic representation generated by $W_0$; irreducibility in the form that every nonzero $F$ in `gl3CyclicSubspace W₀` (the span of the right translates of $W_0$) has $W_0$ in `gl3CyclicSubspace F`; the existence of an open subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ fixing $W_0$ under right translation; and admissibility, namely that for every open subgroup $U_v$ there is a finite set $B$ of functions such that every $U_v$-right-invariant member of `gl3CyclicSubspace W₀` lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of $B$. The hypothesis `hZ` requires central invariance: $W_0\big(g\cdot d\,I_3\big)=W_0(g)$ for every $g$ and every unit $d$ of $\mathbb{Q}_v$ with $|d|=1$ and $|d-1|\le \exp(-\ell)$. A complex number $\varepsilon$ is given together with `hε`: $\varepsilon\neq 0$.
--
--   The analytic input is the hypothesis `hdat`, a family of local functional equations in rational form. It is stated for every $\varpi$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$ whose image $\pi$ in $\mathbb{Q}_v$ is nonzero (`hπ`) of valuation $\exp(-1)$, for all $a_1,a_2\in\mathbb{C}$ with $a_1a_2\neq 0$, and for two functions $W_2,W_2^{\vee}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ subject to normalisation groups of four clauses each: $W_2$ satisfies $W_2(u(x)g)=\psi_v(x)W_2(g)$, is right-invariant under [`AdelicDock.localLevelOne (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ v ⊤`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L178) (the preimage under the local embedding into $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles of the level-one subgroup at the unit ideal), has $W_2(1)=1$, transforms under the central element $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,\pi)$ by the factor $a_1a_2/N$, and has torus values $W_2(\mathrm{diag}(\pi^m,1))=$ `torusFactor N (a₁+a₂) (a₁a₂/N) m` for all $m\in\mathbb{Z}$ (the Hecke recursion sequence $x_0=1$, $x_1=\lambda/N$, $x_{m+2}=(\lambda x_{m+1}-\omega x_m)/N$ for $m\ge 0$, and $0$ for $m<0$); while $W_2^{\vee}$ satisfies the same clauses with $\psi_v^{-1}$ in place of $\psi_v$, central factor $N/(a_1a_2)$, and torus values `torusFactor N (N(a₁+a₂)/(a₁a₂)) (N/(a₁a₂)) m`. The Borel $\sigma$-algebra `localGLBorel ℚ v` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ and the corresponding Borel-space property are installed, after which `hdat` quantifies over all Haar measures $\mu_2$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ and $\mu_N$ on the range of `unipotentGL2Hom` (the upper unipotent subgroup), and over all $W\in$ `gl3CyclicSubspace W₀`. For each such choice it asserts the existence of polynomials $p,q,p^{\vee},q^{\vee}\in\mathbb{C}[X]$ and reals $\sigma_2,\sigma_3$ with $q\neq 0$, $q^{\vee}\neq 0$ and five further clauses, all integrals being taken against $\mu_2$ weighted by [`HaarQuotient.density`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L25) for the unipotent subgroup and $\mu_N$: integrability of $g\mapsto W(\iota(g))W_2(g)\,|\det g|^{\,s-1/2}$ for $\mathrm{Re}\,s>\sigma_2$, where $\iota=$ `iotaGL` is the block embedding $\mathrm{GL}_2\hookrightarrow\mathrm{GL}_3$ and $|\cdot|$ is `modulus`; integrability of $g\mapsto \widetilde{W}\big(\iota(g)\,\iota(\mathrm{diag}(\pi,\pi)^{-\ell})\big)W_2^{\vee}(g)\,|\det g|^{\,1-s-1/2}$ for $\mathrm{Re}(1-s)>\sigma_3$, where $\widetilde{W}=$ `dualWhittakerFn3 W` is $g\mapsto W(w_3\,{}^{t}g^{-1})$ for the long Weyl element $w_3$; the identity `rsLocalIntegral` $\Psi(s,W\circ\iota,W_2)\cdot q(N^{-s})=p(N^{-s})$ for $\mathrm{Re}\,s>\sigma_2$; the dual identity $\Psi\big(1-s,\widetilde{W}(\,\cdot\,\iota(\mathrm{diag}(\pi,\pi)^{-\ell})),W_2^{\vee}\big)\cdot q^{\vee}(N^{-(1-s)})=p^{\vee}(N^{-(1-s)})$ for $\mathrm{Re}(1-s)>\sigma_3$; and, for all $s\in\mathbb{C}$,
--   $$p^{\vee}(N^{-(1-s)})\,q(N^{-s})\,E^{\vee}\big(a_1^{-1}N^{-(1/2-s)}\big)E^{\vee}\big(a_2^{-1}N^{-(1/2-s)}\big) = p(N^{-s})\,q^{\vee}(N^{-(1-s)})\,E\big(a_1N^{-(s+1/2)}\big)E\big(a_2N^{-(s+1/2)}\big)\,\varepsilon^2 .$$
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion asserts the existence of $W\in$ `gl3CyclicSubspace W₀` with three properties. First, $W(g k)=W(g)$ for all $g\in\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ and all $k$ in `congruenceK1 (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ v ℓ`, that is all $k$ whose entries and the entries of $k^{-1}$ have valuation $\le 1$ and which satisfy $|k_{2,0}|\le\exp(-\ell)$, $|k_{2,1}|\le\exp(-\ell)$ and $|k_{2,2}-1|\le\exp(-\ell)$. Second, $W(1)=1$. Third, for every $\varpi$ with nonzero image $\pi$ of valuation $\exp(-1)$, all $a_1,a_2$ with $a_1a_2\neq 0$, every $W_2$ satisfying the five normalisation clauses listed above ($\psi_v$-equivariance under the unipotent, right invariance under [`AdelicDock.localLevelOne (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ v ⊤`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L178), $W_2(1)=1$, central factor $a_1a_2/N$, and the `torusFactor` values), and — with the same Borel structure installed — all Haar measures $\mu_2$ and $\mu_N$ as above, there exists $\sigma_2\in\mathbb{R}$ such that for $\mathrm{Re}\,s>\sigma_2$ the function $g\mapsto W(\iota(g))W_2(g)\,|\det g|^{\,s-1/2}$ is integrable against the density-weighted measure, and for $\mathrm{Re}\,s>\sigma_2$
--   $$\Psi\big(s,\,W\circ\iota,\,W_2\big)\cdot E\big(a_1N^{-(s+1/2)}\big)\cdot E\big(a_2N^{-(s+1/2)}\big) \;=\; \operatorname{vol}\big(\{g:\exists\,n\in\mathrm{range}(\mathrm{unipotentGL2Hom}),\ \exists\,k\in\mathrm{AdelicDock.localLevelOne}\,\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}\,\mathbb{Q}\,v\,\top,\ g=nk\}\big),$$
--   where $\Psi$ is [`RSCarrier.rsLocalIntegral`](def/LanglandsTunnell_RSCarrier.html#L16) for the data $(\mu_2,\ \mathrm{range}(\mathrm{unipotentGL2Hom}),\ \mu_N,\ g\mapsto|\det g|)$ and the right-hand side is the measure of that product set under $\mu_2$ weighted by [`HaarQuotient.density`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L25), passed to $\mathbb{R}$ by `toReal` and then to $\mathbb{C}$. In particular the resulting vector has no dual-side clause, no polynomials and no $\varepsilon$ in its characterisation: its local Rankin–Selberg integral is exactly the constant $\operatorname{vol}(NK)$ divided by the two induced Euler factors.
--
--   This is the local newvector extraction step of the cubic-induction argument used in the Langlands–Tunnell converse-theorem input: at a place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ unramified in the cubic field $K$ but above which the twisting character $\mu$ ramifies, the rational local $\mathrm{GL}_3\times\mathrm{GL}_2$ functional equations force the cyclic space of the given Whittaker datum to contain a vector invariant under the congruence subgroup $K_1$ of level $\ell$, normalised at the identity, whose local integral against every normalised spherical $\mathrm{GL}_2$ Whittaker function is the expected volume constant divided by the induced Euler factors. It is used by [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_mem_gl3CyclicSubspace_congruenceK1_torusValues_of_isCubicInductionDataOn`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_mem_gl3CyclicSubspace_congruenceK1_torusValues_of_isCubicInductionDataOn).
